---
const repoScaffolding = ['VADFactory', 'PyAnnote dependencies', 'lazy get_vad() helper'];
const activePath = [
  'Buffered audio reaches process_buffer()',
  'model.transcribe() runs without the VAD path being invoked first',
  'Returned segments reach CaptionControl.vue',
  'Client keeps text only when no_speech_prob ≤ 0.6 and temperature ≤ 0.8',
];
---

<figure class="filtering-truth not-prose">
  <header>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Repository truth vs runtime truth</p>
      <h3>VAD infrastructure exists, but the current public streaming path does not use it before Whisper.</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="badge">Do not overstate</span>
  </header>

  <div class="truth-grid">
    <section class="present">
      <div class="section-label">Present in repository</div>
      <ul>
        {repoScaffolding.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>These pieces show intended or available VAD scaffolding, not active silence dropping in the current public transcription path.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="active">
      <div class="section-label">Active path in current public source</div>
      <ol>
        {activePath.map((item, index) => (
          <li>
            <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <p>{item}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="boundary">
    <span>Behavioral boundary</span>
    <strong>Client-side probabilistic filtering reduces likely low-confidence output; it does not guarantee all phantom transcription is eliminated.</strong>
  </div>

  <figcaption>The distinction is source-grounded: available architecture and active runtime behavior are not the same claim.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .filtering-truth {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.7rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .filtering-truth :global(p),
  .filtering-truth :global(h3),
  .filtering-truth :global(ol),
  .filtering-truth :global(ul),
  .filtering-truth :global(li) { margin: 0; }

  .filtering-truth :global(ol),
  .filtering-truth :global(ul) { padding: 0; list-style: none; }

  header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .badge,
  .section-label,
  .active li > span,
  .boundary > span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.54rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-top: 0.45rem !important;
    max-width: 47rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.47rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .truth-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .truth-grid section {
    min-width: 0;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .truth-grid .active {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 4%, var(--bg-card));
  }

  .section-label {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.49rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .active .section-label { color: var(--accent); }

  .present ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
  }

  .present li {
    border-left: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
  }

  .present > p {
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .active ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
  }

  .active li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    min-height: 2.9rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: 0.55rem 0.65rem;
  }

  .active li > span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.47rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .active li p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .boundary {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
  }

  .boundary > span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.47rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .boundary strong {
    max-width: 52rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  figcaption {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .truth-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    header { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  }
</style>